BT /F1 20 Tf 50 720 Td (DeepPDF: Advanced Retrieval Strategies in RAG Systems) Tj 0 -30 Td /F2 12 Tf (Authors: Kesav Satya Sai, AI Research Lab) Tj 0 -25 Td (Abstract) Tj 0 -15 Td /F3 10 Tf (Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) combines parametric memory with external non-parametric retrieval.) Tj 0 -15 Td (Standard dense retrieval suffers from vocabulary mismatch, lost-in-the-middle phenomena, and low keyword fidelity.) Tj 0 -15 Td (This paper introduces DeepPDF, a benchmarked framework comparing 7 advanced retrieval techniques.) Tj 0 -30 Td /F2 12 Tf (1. Dense Vector Retrieval Baseline) Tj 0 -15 Td /F3 10 Tf (Dense retrieval maps document chunks into a continuous embedding space using sentence transformers.) Tj 0 -15 Td (Cosine similarity is computed: sim(q, d) = (q . d) / (||q|| * ||d||). Typical dimensionality is 384 dims.) Tj 0 -30 Td /F2 12 Tf (2. BM25 Lexical Keyword Search) Tj 0 -15 Td /F3 10 Tf (BM25 evaluates term frequency (TF) and inverse document frequency (IDF) with length normalization.) Tj 0 -15 Td (Parameters k1=1.5 and b=0.75 govern saturation and document length penalties.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
